*  empty.sno -- the null string, assigned and tested.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
*
*  An assignment with nothing on the right gives the null string, and
*  IDENT and DIFFER are how you ask. Both are written each time round;
*  the one that does not apply fails, and a statement that fails
*  prints nothing, so the output is what was true.
        S =
        OUTPUT = IDENT(S) 'null string: empty'
        OUTPUT = DIFFER(S) 'null string: not empty'
        OUTPUT = 'its size is ' SIZE(S)
*
        S = 'x'
        OUTPUT = IDENT(S) 'one character: empty'
        OUTPUT = DIFFER(S) 'one character: not empty'
        OUTPUT = 'its size is ' SIZE(S)
END
